From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XuanTie Linux SDK CI <noreply@linux.alibaba.com>
Date: Sat, 2 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] six: add find_spec to vendored six importer for Python 3.13

poetry-core 1.0.8 prepends its bundled _vendor directory to sys.path[0]
(poetry/core/__init__.py), so every bare `import six` resolves to the
vendored six 1.15.0 rather than the system python3-six 1.16.0. That
1.15.0 ships a _SixMetaPathImporter that only implements the legacy
find_module()/load_module() finder protocol and has no find_spec().

Since CPython 3.12 the import system no longer falls back to a meta path
finder's legacy find_module() (importlib._bootstrap._find_spec only calls
finder.find_spec and skips finders lacking it). The six.moves virtual
namespace therefore never gets registered and any vendored consumer that
does `from six.moves import ...` (poetry.core itself, the vendored
pyrsistent and jsonschema, etc.) fails on python3 3.13 with:

    ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'six.moves'

Backport the fix upstream six shipped in 1.16.0: give the importer
find_spec()/create_module()/exec_module() (importlib Loader protocol) and
the spec_from_loader import. This restores the six.moves namespace for all
consumers at once, instead of rewriting each call site. Behaviour on
Python <= 3.11 is unchanged (spec_from_loader is imported defensively).

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/benjaminp/six commit 6c8dcc1 ; vendored copy]
---
--- a/poetry/core/_vendor/six.py
+++ b/poetry/core/_vendor/six.py
@@ -31,6 +31,11 @@
 __author__ = "Benjamin Peterson <benjamin@python.org>"
 __version__ = "1.15.0"
 
+try:
+    from importlib.util import spec_from_loader
+except ImportError:
+    spec_from_loader = None
+
 
 # Useful for very coarse version differentiation.
 PY2 = sys.version_info[0] == 2
@@ -186,6 +191,11 @@
             return self
         return None
 
+    def find_spec(self, fullname, path, target=None):
+        if fullname in self.known_modules:
+            return spec_from_loader(fullname, self)
+        return None
+
     def __get_module(self, fullname):
         try:
             return self.known_modules[fullname]
@@ -223,6 +233,12 @@
         return None
     get_source = get_code  # same as get_code
 
+    def create_module(self, spec):
+        return self.load_module(spec.name)
+
+    def exec_module(self, module):
+        pass
+
 _importer = _SixMetaPathImporter(__name__)
 
 
